BASE = """Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: one complete portrait mobile hero-defense battlefield environment concept, no UI. Single continuous map filling the image; approximately 2:3 portrait, viewed from the same overhead-oblique 2D camera as the existing maps.
Input images: Image 1 is the ONLY allowed prop/vegetation/rock asset catalog for this biome. Image 2 shows our four existing maps as camera, scale, composition and drawing-style reference. Use the sprites in Image 1 as the actual art vocabulary: preserve their recognizable silhouettes, flat colors, outlines, small ground shadows and chunky proportions; arrange and repeat them, do not replace them with unrelated concept-art objects. Never copy catalog labels or the editorial frames.
Primary request: {biome} biome, concept {number}, {title}.
Composition: {layout} Keep roughly 60 percent of the image as quiet connected walkable combat ground, with room for around twenty distributed defensive-building positions without drawing any pads or buildings. Leave broad approaches on more than one map edge. Scenery should frame and divide the arena naturally, matching the spacious existing maps. Do not turn the battlefield into a thin winding road. Show the whole map from above, no sky and no horizon.
Palette and source props: {palette}
Only allowed missing-art additions: {terrain}. These are terrain/shoreline extensions absent from the source pack, drawn in exactly the simple flat, faceted map style of Image 2. All trees, bushes, rocks and small details must remain from Image 1's visual families. Keep trees and props at game-map scale, not gigantic scenic illustration scale.
Style: clean hand-drawn mobile-game 2D sprites, crisp consistent outlines, two or three flat cel-shaded tones, restrained simple shadows, very little surface detail. Clear readable silhouettes, no realistic lighting, no painterly brush texture, no 3D render. Maintain the same neutral daylight and vertical map framing as Image 2.
Text: none. No labels, numbers, titles, watermarks, border, legend, debug lines, wireframes, grid, green placement pads, characters, enemies, towers, gates, buildings, HUD or perspective camera tilt. Deliver one finished environment concept, not a contact sheet or variations grid."""

existing_manifest = ROOT / "concept-jobs.json"
if existing_manifest.exists() and any(j.get("status") == "generated" for j in json.loads(existing_manifest.read_text())):
    raise RuntimeError("Completed concepts already exist; use a new output folder instead of resetting their manifest")
jobs = []
for biome_id, (biome_name, palette, variants) in BRIEFS.items():
    (ROOT / biome_id).mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    for number, (slug, layout, terrain) in enumerate(variants, 1):
        title = slug.replace("-", " ").title()
        prompt = BASE.format(biome=biome_name, number=number, title=title, layout=layout, palette=palette, terrain=terrain)
        jobs.append({"id": f"{biome_id}-{number:02d}", "biome": biome_id, "biomeName": biome_name, "number": number,
                     "title": title, "file": f"{biome_id}/{number:02d}-{slug}.png", "prompt": prompt,
                     "references": [str(ROOT / "references" / (biome_id + "-source-board.png")), str(ROOT / "references" / "current-four-maps.png")],
                     "allowedTerrainAdditions": terrain, "status": "pending"})
(ROOT / "concept-jobs.json").write_text(json.dumps(jobs, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
(ROOT / "prompts.txt").write_text("\n\n".join("=== " + j["id"] + " | " + j["title"] + " ===\n" + j["prompt"] for j in jobs) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
print(f"Prepared {len(jobs)} separate OpenAI image-generation prompts")
